# Cache rules for the deployed assets.
#
# Cloudflare's asset handler sends `Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate` for
# everything. Measured on this deployment, those responses carry NO ETag and no
# Last-Modified, so with `max-age=0` the browser has nothing to revalidate against and
# re-downloads the whole file on every visit - which is what the old single-file page did
# with its 188 KB.
#
# The filenames below contain a hash of their own contents, so a given URL can never serve
# different bytes. That is what makes it safe to say "keep it forever": when the code
# changes, the filename changes and the browser fetches the new one.
#
# The shell keeps the default rule on purpose: it is the file that names the current hashes,
# so it is the one thing that must always be re-checked.
#
# NOTE: Cloudflare parses this file, and its comment character is `#`. A C-style comment
# here is read as a URL rule followed by malformed headers, and the deploy FAILS - which is
# how it was discovered.
/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31556952, immutable
